use std
into look.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's theme, contrast, and glanceable car typography module. Every color is an ARGB unsigned 32-bit integer (alpha in the top byte). All floating-point math uses 32-bit floats.
Struct `Preset` holds `key` and `label` as growable byte buffers, `bg` and `accent` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `light` as a boolean. Every field has a default (empty buffers, zero, false).
Struct `Palette` holds `bg`, `panel`, `panel2`, `line`, `line2`, `acc`, `ink`, `soft`, `dim`, `gold`, `err`, and `ok` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `light` as a boolean.
Struct `TypeScale` holds `telemetry_px`, `title_px`, `button_px`, `body_px`, `meta_px`, `min_hit_px`, `gutter_px`, and `pad_px` as 32-bit floats.
Function `presets` takes no arguments and returns a growable list of `Preset` values in this order, built once into a module cache.
```table preset_rows Preset
